These posts concern two- and three-year-olds whose play competes with a necessary adult task or a need for silence. Activities may require help after five or ten minutes, make too much mess, or leave the parent worried about supervision. One parent reports fitting a bathroom visit into hide-and-seek rather than asking for a new activity.

