## Pattern 2, share 03: across the yes posts

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 69 of 80 |
| others | 29 of 80 |
| bought | 2 of 80 |
| feeling | 43 of 80 |

Tags count what is stated in the share, once per post. Tried includes existing routines and reported attempts; others includes reported advice, actions and comparisons involving people beyond the focal child. Bought requires a stated purchase or payment: ownership, enrollment, intended spending and free resources alone do not establish it. Feeling requires a stated adult feeling or self-assessment, not just the child’s emotion; the fictional toddler voice is not treated as an adult feeling.

### What they tried, in their words

- "Coloring books — good for about 5 minutes then she wants help
Play doh — mess situation if I am not watching
Sticker books — she loves them but burns through fast
Kinetic sand — tried once, never again
Magnetic board on the wall — still going, maybe 2 months in
Kids podcasts — hit or miss, depends on her mood
Small world play (animals and a tray) — works well but takes setup
Duplo — decent but she wants me to build with her after 10 minutes" [ar079-0005]
- "Here are the things we usually do: playground time, the water table in our backyard, watering plants, helping me garden, and taking walks around the neighborhood so she can play with sticks, rocks, leaves, etc. She also loves going to the lake to look for animals and bugs." [ar035-0006]
- "The first 3 days were rough. He asked for the tablet every single morning, sometimes multiple times. I felt terrible saying no every time especially when i was trying to get myself ready and out the door. I filled the gap with random stuff around the house. His wooden magnet board, books, a bowl of dried pasta he could pour between cups which sounds ridiculous but somehow bought me 20 minutes." [ar012-0047]
- "The water table has saved me honestly! Maybe I’ll take more toys out onto the balcony and have her wash things, thank you!" [ar009-0068]
- "We've done it every single morning this week. The concentration on her face is unreal. I've started just quietly setting it up before she wakes up because I know it's coming." [ar065-0035]
- "I have always rotated toys, most all are open ended, some are not. He has a climbing tower that he doesn't mess with. I always have to initiate any play even with the toys he does like." [ar027-0093]
- "We started running around 2.5, but he was easily distracted. The past few weeks he knows that if he wants to run he has to do it since it's part of the workout. He also does pushups with me. He gets really focused when a timer is running and other people are doing the workout." [ar006-0102]
- "[…]We have been offering quiet time instead. That’s fine, she has a good time poking around her room. Books and quiet toys.[…]" [ar031-0061]
- "Yesterday we actually had a pretty good day, I put him in the burley and biked him around the neighborhood for about 30 mins then we stopped at a playground and did the swings for a long time. It was hard to keep him off the rest of the equipment but he seemed pretty satisfied with just swinging. I was planning the same thing for today but turns out it's storming all day :(" [ar012-0079]
- "It's an easier way to get maximum tickle effect without having to bend down or get on the ground myself. He absolutely cracks up and loves it. You know I'd do anything to get those belly laughs!" [ar001-0068]

### What other people told them or did

- "[…]My MIL worked in education but she’s no help here cause all she says is « she’s just a baby she needs you » yes and?[…]" [ar065-0040]
- "I’m actually not sure I would know this except that a friend went down a slide with their 2 year old daughter and her leg ended up broken.  So I will never ride down a slide with my child.  I did know whatever happened was safer without me in the slide." [ar084-0007]
- "[…]My husband thinks the fighting is harmless fun and a safe place for her to have free fun since no one is actually harmed." [ar056-0101]
